TEXT 176 16 Left 2 !.ac list 50 50.1
TEXT -8 -472 Left 5 ;NOTE: In this examples only the inductive coupling is considered\nThe impedance depends of the current flow in the other line !!!!\nVoltages are transported via the inductance, currents are driven\nImpedances are small\nIn contrast the transformer: Voltages are driven, Currents are transported,\nImpedances are high
TEXT 304 296 Left 2 !.param PN=10e6 QN=0
TEXT 120 104 Left 2 ;Z1=Z2=Z3=1 \nSymmetric operation mode\nsame results like in the uncoupled case
TEXT 504 120 Left 2 ;Coupling is here near 1\nZ1=Z2=Z3= almost zero
TEXT 864 112 Left 2 ;Asymmetric operation mode:\nZ1=1.6\nZ2=2\nZ3=2\nV at the starpoint 400mV/-90
TEXT 1240 112 Left 2 ;Same phase operation mode\n (e.g 3 phase short circuit current\n with fault at another line)\nZ1=4\nZ2=4\nZ3=4\nU at the starpoint 2mV/-90
TEXT 248 344 Left 2 ;Z1=Z2=Z3=1 \nSymmetric case\nresults like in uncoupled case
TEXT 776 344 Left 2 ;Z1=Z2=Z3=1 \nSymmetric case\nwithout coupling
TEXT 0 -80 Left 2 ;Symmetric operation mode:\nZ1,Z2=1 (V1/I1,V2/I2)\nV1=1V I1=1A\nV2=-1V I2=-1A\nCoupling k=XM12*sqrt(X1*X2)->XM12=1 (X1,X2=2,k=0.5)\nComputation:\nV1=X1*I1+XM12*I2=2*1-1*1=1V\nV2=X2*I2+XM12*I1=-2*1+1.1=-1V
TEXT 456 -64 Left 2 ;Symmetric operation mode:\nline above is open\nZ2=2ohm V2=2 I2=1A V1=1V (k=0.5)
TEXT 512 -168 Left 2 ;V1=1V
TEXT 1208 -56 Left 2 ;Same phase operation mode:\nZ1=3ohm V1=3V I1=1A\nZ2=3ohm V2=3V I2=1A
TEXT 1600 -40 Left 2 ;Same phase operation mode: (e.g fault current)\nZ1=12ohm V1=12V I1=1A\nZ2=2.1ohm V2=21V I2=10A
TEXT 1504 -48 Left 2 !.param AC1=1\n.param AC2=10
TEXT -304 -136 Left 5 ;1 phase current driven
TEXT -312 96 Left 5 ;1 phase current driven\nphase shift 0 degrees or\n180 degrees
TEXT -8 -312 Left 5 ;In all examples k=0.5
TEXT 808 -56 Left 2 ;Asymmetric operation mode:\nZ1=1.5ohm V1=3V I1=2A\nZ2=0ohm V2=0.750V I2=-1A
TEXT 512 -120 Left 2 ;V2=1V
TEXT -8 -200 Left 2 ;V1=Voltage on Z1\nV2=Voltage on Z2\nFor differential measurement Click on the left line than hold and drag to the second line
TEXT 1640 376 Left 2 ;Z1=Z2=Z3=1 \nAsymmetric operation case uncoupled with fault in phase 3\n V1=42V!!! I1=42.6A\n V2=42V!!! I2=42.6A\n V3=69.2kV I3=69.3kA
TEXT 1776 432 Left 2 ;Short circuit voltage phase and current phase \nU=120°\n I=120°-90°=30°
TEXT 1728 288 Left 5 ;69kA
TEXT 1136 376 Left 2 ;Asymmetric case with fault in phase 3\nZ1=775ohm V1=34.6kV I1=44.6A\nZ2=775ohm V2=34.6kV I2=44.6A\nZ3=2.0ohm V3=69.2kV I3=34.6kA
TEXT 1288 432 Left 2 ;Short circuit voltage phase and current phase \nU=120°\n I=120°-90°=30°
TEXT 1184 280 Left 5 ;34.5kA
TEXT 1456 224 Left 2 ;Here you can see big differences\nof the line voltages between coupled and uncoupled case\nThe fault current is at the right side two times the curent at the left side\nThe voltage increase (appr.30kv in Phase1,2) is not seen \nat the right side
TEXT 416 248 Left 2 ;In the symmetric operation case\nthere is no difference if the lines\nare coupled or not
TEXT -320 320 Left 5 ;3 phase symmetric operation\nand error operation (1 phase)
TEXT 168 376 Left 4 ;coupled
TEXT 1208 424 Left 4 ;coupled
TEXT 688 384 Left 4 ;uncoupled
TEXT 1744 408 Left 4 ;uncoupled
TEXT 1672 112 Left 2 ;Same phase operation mode\n (e.g 3 phase short circuit current\n with fault at another line)\nZ1=1\nZ2=1\nZ3=1\nU at the starpoint 500mV/-90
TEXT 1176 32 Left 4 ;coupled
TEXT 1608 32 Left 4 ;uncoupled
